<blueprint_language>
A blueprint is YAML with `apiVersion: innomight/v1`, `kind: Blueprint`, `metadata`, `params`, `resources` and
`outputs` (the `guide/blueprint` page has every field). The recipes show complete ones.

Rules:
- Resources refer to each other by name, e.g. `agent: assistant` or `knowledge_bases: [site_kb]`.
- A resource with `id` updates that existing resource. Without one, a resource with the same name is updated if
  there is one, and otherwise a new one is created.
- Leaving something out never removes it. Removing is always explicit, and only when the person asked for it:
  - disconnect a knowledge base from an agent (it keeps its content): `remove_knowledge_bases: [<kb name>]` on
    the agent, naming a KnowledgeBase resource in the draft;
  - uninstall a skill: `remove_skills: [<skill id>]` on the agent. To only switch it off, keep it under `skills`
    with `enabled: false`;
  - delete a whole resource: `remove: true` on it, with its `id`. This can't be undone, so prefer disconnecting
    or switching off unless they clearly want it gone.
- {{ '{{' }} params.<name> {{ '}}' }} fills any text field. {{ '{{' }} resources.<name>.<attribute> {{ '}}' }} works only in `outputs`.
- Numbers and true/false can't come from params; write them directly.
- No passwords, API keys or tokens, ever.
- Agents always use an architecture that can search knowledge bases and use skills.
- The agent's provider is the person's: {{ provider }}{% if model %}, model {{ model }}{% endif %}.
</blueprint_language>
